    {
      "skill_id": "fr-a1-018",
      "title": "Short commands: the imperative",
      "explanation": "The imperative is the present-tense verb without the subject. For -er verbs the tu form loses its final -s: tu parles becomes Parle ! The vous form is Parlez ! and the nous form means let's: Parlons ! Être is irregular: sois, soyons, soyez. For a negative command put ne ... pas around the verb: Ne parle pas ! Add s'il te plaît (to a friend) or s'il vous plaît (polite or plural) to make a request polite.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Écoute, s'il te plaît.",
          "en": "Listen, please."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Mangeons ensemble !",
          "en": "Let's eat together."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Ne parlez pas ici.",
          "en": "Do not speak here."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["FEI-INV"],
