    {
      "skill_id": "fr-a1-019",
      "title": "Near future with aller + infinitive",
      "explanation": "To say what is going to happen soon, use the present tense of aller followed by an infinitive: Je vais travailler. Elle va arriver. Nous allons voyager. The conjugated verb is aller (vais, vas, va, allons, allez, vont) and the second verb never changes. Time words help: demain (tomorrow), ce soir (tonight), bientôt (soon) and la semaine prochaine (next week). In a negative sentence ne ... pas goes around aller: Je ne vais pas travailler.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Je vais regarder un film ce soir.",
          "en": "I am going to watch a film tonight."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Elle va arriver bientôt.",
          "en": "She is going to arrive soon."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Nous allons voyager demain.",
          "en": "We are going to travel tomorrow."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["FEI-INV"],
